---
title: 'Combination Charts'
description: 'Create $framework Combination Charts by combining two or more series types for more flexible data visualisations. Add a secondary axis to handle different scales.'
---

A combination chart combines two or more series types allowing for flexible data visualisations. They are ideal for making visual comparisons of different sets of data in a single chart.

## Combination Series Types

Series types can be combined with other series types used in the same kind of chart:

- **Cartesian charts**: `bar`, `line`, `area`, `scatter`, `bubble`, `histogram`, `range-bar`, `range-area`, `box-plot`, `candlestick`, `hlc` and `ohlc`.
- **Polar charts**: `radar-line`, `radar-area` and `nightingale`.
- **Pie and donut charts**: `pie` and `donut`.

The `type` property must be specified explicitly on each individual series object in the `series` options array, as shown below:

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'bar', // use 'bar' series
            xKey: 'year',
            yKey: 'men',
            // ...other series options
        },
        {
            type: 'line', // use 'line' series
            xKey: 'year',
            yKey: 'portions',
            // ...other series options
        },
    ],
}
```

The snippet above shows the configuration required for a combination chart consisting of a `bar` and `line` series.

The example below demonstrates two common combination chart types. You can switch between these two combination chart types using the buttons above the chart. Please note:

- Series are rendered according to the order in which they are added in the `series` array.
- The area and line series are plotted on a [Secondary Axis](./axes-secondary/) with a different scale.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Combination Charts" name="combination" type="generated" /%}

### Restrictions

- Series types used in different kinds of chart cannot be combined. For example, a `bar` series cannot be combined with a `radar-line` series. The first series in the `series` array determines the kind of chart, and any series that doesn't suit it is ignored.
- The following series types cannot be combined with any other series. If one of them is the first series in the `series` array, only that series is processed. Otherwise, it is ignored:
    - [`waterfall`](./waterfall-series/), [`funnel`](./funnel-series/) and [`cone-funnel`](./cone-funnel-series/)
    - [`pyramid`](./pyramid-series/), [`sankey`](./sankey-series/), [`sunburst`](./sunburst-series/), [`treemap`](./treemap-series/), [`chord`](./chord-series/) and [`organization`](./org-chart/)
    - [`radial-gauge`](./radial-gauge/) and [`linear-gauge`](./linear-gauge/)

